@page "/products"

<PageTitle>Products</PageTitle>

<h1>Products</h1>

<p class="page-intro">
    HamBus Suite currently includes one flagship desktop product, with this web project ready to host richer suite content over time.
</p>

<div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card product-card">
        <div class="product-card-header">
            <span class="status-pill status-live">Live</span>
            <h2>HamBusLog</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            The current HamBus desktop application for QSO logging, contest workflows, DX spot monitoring,
            rig control, and import/export operations.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Avalonia desktop UI</li>
            <li>SQLite and PostgreSQL-backed persistence support</li>
            <li>WSJT-X auto-log integration and duplicate handling</li>
            <li>Contest-aware entry and Cabrillo export</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/static/hambuslog.html">Static product page</a>
        </div>
    </article>

    <article class="feature-card product-card">
        <div class="product-card-header">
            <span class="status-pill status-planned">Foundation</span>
            <h2>HamBusWeb</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            This new web project gives the suite a place for landing pages, docs, download instructions,
            and future interactive experiences such as dashboards or account-backed features.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Blazor Server rendering for interactive pages</li>
            <li>Plain static HTML under <code>wwwroot</code></li>
            <li>Ready for future product pages and documentation</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/static/index.html">See static-site guide</a>
        </div>
    </article>
</div>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Next likely additions</h2>
        <p>Common uses for the suite site as the product family grows.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
            <h3>Documentation hub</h3>
            <p>Setup guides, contest workflows, release notes, and troubleshooting content.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
            <h3>Download center</h3>
            <p>Published builds, package instructions, and version-specific notes for each platform.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
            <h3>Suite expansion</h3>
            <p>Future HamBus tools can each get their own product page without changing the site architecture.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
